## Astro Frontmatter TypeScript Rules
- Frontmatter runs at build/request time — no browser APIs (`window`, `document`)
- Use `Astro.props` with typed interface — always define `interface Props`
- Use `Astro.url`, `Astro.site`, `Astro.locals` — all are typed
- For client-side code, use `<script>` tags in template or `client:*` islands

```astro
---
// ✅ Correct frontmatter
interface Props {
  title: string;
  count?: number;
}
const { title, count = 0 } = Astro.props; // Fully typed

// ❌ Wrong — browser API in frontmatter
const path = window.location.pathname; // ReferenceError at build time
---
```
